title: Payers › Rules & Instructions › Mark a rule as verified
route: /payers/summit?tab=rules
intro: 'Mark as verified' is the only way a rule becomes Verified. A person names the source and the date they checked it; Psyflo cannot check a source itself and says so. An address is optional and must be a web address. Nothing is opened or fetched. Editing a rule never verifies it, and editing a verified rule sends it back to Needs review. Verification is a record of what a person did, not a payer's confirmation.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Open a rule row\nclick 'Mark as verified'\n('Verify again' on a verified rule)"
overlay m "Mark as verified\n'Verified means a person checked it against a source.\nPsyflo does not check the source itself.'"
input i1 "Type 'Source' (required)\nExample: the payer's provider manual, section 4, or a call reference"
input i2 "Type 'Source address' (optional)\nhttps://..."
input i3 "Pick 'Source published on' (optional date)"
input i4 "Pick 'Checked on' (required date)\nStarts as today in the demo (Oct 20, 2026)"
click ok "Click 'Mark as verified'"
decision d1 "Is the source empty?"
toast e1 "'Name the source: the payer's manual, a letter, a call reference.'"
decision d2 "Is there an address that does not start with http:// or https://?"
toast e2 "'Use a web address that starts with http:// or https://, or leave it empty.'"
decision d3 "Is the date missing or after today?"
toast e3 "'Add the date you checked it.'\nor 'That date is in the future. Use today or earlier.'"
store st "Rule saved as Verified\nSource label, address and publication date kept\nLast verified = the date entered\nVersion goes up by one, one history line"
store lg "Edit audit gets a 'Rules' line\n'Verified against the source ...' with your name and the time"
screen out "Row shows a green 'Verified' pill\n'Source: ...' (a link when it has an address)\n'Last verified Oct 20, 2026'\nThe 'unverified' note is gone"
process wf "Workflows that use the rule read it as verified\nTest Workflow no longer warns that it is unverified"
process nv "Nothing else becomes verified\nA payer's other rules, and a rule edited later, keep their own state"
click cx "Click 'Cancel', the X or press Escape"
endx x1 "Pop-up closes\nNothing changed"
end e1b "The rule is Verified, with a source and a date"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Test a workflow"
goto g2 "Continues in: Payers › Edit log"

s1 --> m --> i1 --> i2 --> i3 --> i4 --> ok --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| e1 --> i1
d1 -->|No| d2
d2 -->|Yes| e2 --> i2
d2 -->|No| d3
d3 -->|Yes| e3 --> i4
d3 -->|No| st --> lg --> out --> wf --> nv --> e1b
m --> cx --> x1
lg -.-> g2
wf -.-> g1
